      <h1 class="ed-title">Treadmill After Hip Replacement</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        The American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons says it is safe to walk on a treadmill after a hip replacement if you are worried about uneven ground outside. The details that matter are when you start, how your hip precautions apply on the belt, and how you get on and off.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
